Title: COLD HANDOFF
Author: Rachel Stein
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL 4 - NIGHT

Rain hammers the concrete. AGENT LENA CROSS, 40s, waits beside a silver SUV. She checks her watch — 11:58 PM. A BLACK DUFFEL sits at her feet.
LENA
Package is clean. Where's your courier?

INT. PARKING GARAGE - STAIRWELL - NIGHT

Footsteps echo down. DMITRI VOLKOV, 50s, limps into the light, one hand pressed to his ribs. Blood on his sleeve.
DMITRI
They made me at the bridge. Two blocks behind me.
LENA
Then we don't stand here admiring your tailoring.

INT. SILVER SUV - MOVING - NIGHT

Lena drives hard. Dmitri opens the duffel — stacks of microfilm canisters. Headlights flare in the rearview.
DMITRI
If they take this back, a city dies tomorrow.
LENA
It's not even eleven yet. Nobody takes anything. Not on my watch.

EXT. RIVER ROAD OVERPASS - NIGHT

The SUV screeches to a stop. Lena shoves the gray duffel into a maintenance hatch beneath the guardrail. A black sedan closes fast behind them.
LENA
When I say go, you go over the rail. Swim south.

INT. SILVER SUV - NIGHT

The sedan rams their bumper. Lena meets Dmitri's eyes — no sentiment, pure calculus. She reaches for the door.
LENA
Go.

FADE OUT.


THE END
